From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:45:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Keep the MSI_LITE2 bus matrix gate
 running

The USB0 and USB1 host controllers, the USB3 controller and PCIe sit
behind the MSI_LITE2 bus bridge. Nothing in the device tree consumes the
MBUS gate of the bridge, so clk_disable_unused() closes it. The
controllers then no longer reach memory: the EHCI and OHCI registers
still answer, but every transfer times out and no device enumerates.

Mark the gate critical, as is done for the MSI_LITE0 bridge and the
MBUS gate of the storage bridge.

Not covered: describing the bridge gate as a parent of the gates behind
it.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; MBUS_MAT bit 31
(mbus-msi-lite2) reads 1 and the gate is still enabled after the unused
clocks are closed, and the hub on the USB-A port and a stick behind it
enumerate and read without errors.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
index 730237d5a604..efcf5ff0def7 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -603,7 +603,7 @@ static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(mbus_store_clk, "mbus-store", mbus_hws,
 static const struct clk_hw *mbus_store_hws[] = { &mbus_store_clk.common.hw };
 
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(mbus_msi_lite2_clk, "mbus-msi-lite2", mbus_hws,
-			  0x5e0, BIT(31), 0);
+			  0x5e0, BIT(31), CLK_IS_CRITICAL);
 
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(mbus_dma0_clk, "mbus-dma0", mbus_hws,
 			  0x5e4, BIT(0), 0);
